OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Sat 21 Nov to Mon 30 Nov
OL,6,FBands of rain will move in from the
OL,7,FAtlantic at times, making erratic and
OL,8,Funcertain eastward progress across the
OL,9,FUK. These systems may also bring
OL,10,Foccasional strong winds. Either side
OL,11,Fof bands of rain a mixture of clear/
OL,12,Fsunny spells and showers. Often rather
OL,13,Fcold in northern areas which could
OL,14,Fallow precipitation to fall as snow at
OL,15,Ftimes, mainly over hills. Generally
OL,16,Fmilder in the south though still
OL,17,Fpotential for some nights in clearer
OL,18,Fspells. Through late November, there
OL,19,Fis an increasing chance that high
OL,20,Fpressure will start to have more
OL,21,Finfluence bringing more settled
OL,22,Fconditions, particularly across the
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Fnorth.
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
FL,164,160,301,260,100,100
PN,16303
SC,0003
CT,20,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F163A1794918748
OL,1,Wj5hw1~{4k7juhw1{$             G3/3
OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Tue 1 Dec to Tue 15 DecFThe
OL,6,Ftrack of low pressure systems will
OL,7,Flikely be further south than normal
OL,8,Fduring this period. This means that
OL,9,Frainfall will probably be focussed
OL,10,Facross the south of the UK;
OL,11,Fconversely, higher pressure to the
OL,12,Fnorth means drier conditions here.
OL,13,FTemperatures in the south will
OL,14,Fprobably be near normal or perhaps
OL,15,Fslightly above at times, with the
OL,16,Fnorth colder than normal.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
